WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.300
Every reader keeps a shelf.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.300
Meet the modern, digital one.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.000
52 books, two languages, 14,000 pages.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.100
Every book is a spine.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.800
Width is pages, colour is subject, and a ribbon

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.833
means a review.

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:21.400
Run a finger along the shelf, and each one

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.300
tips out.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.733
Six ways to shelve it.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.467
Every book walks to its place.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:30.600
Filter, and nothing vanishes.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.633
The rest just dim.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.333
Or turn the shelf face out.

00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:37.800
Can't choose?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.600
Pull one for me.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.800
Four more lenses:

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.767
the slip, the numbers, the lines I kept, the

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:46.600
catalogue.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.667
By day, or after dark.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.067
Classic, or atlas.

00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:54.067
The Reading Room.

00:00:54.733 --> 00:00:59.433
Come, take one down, at sankettambare.in/books.
